==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Butterfly Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Fishman Cat''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
With good speed and Massive Damage to Floating, Swimmer can quickly approach and gravely cripple or outright delete certain [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] enemies such as [[Mooth]], [[Owlbrow]] and [[The Face]], or to deal chip damage against non-Floating threats like [[Cruel Angel Clionel]]. Even at a range disadvantage, Swimmer is still usually able to land a hit and score a lot of damage, as its full backswing cooldown causes it to attack again if it gets displaced to enemy attacks/Knockback effects but survives. However, matchups against common [[Teacher Bun Bun|Teacher]] [[J.K. Bun Bun|Bun]] [[Bun Bun Black|Bun]] [[Bun Bun Symbiote|variants]] are risky as it is outranged by them, of which can be dealt with much more effectively by its more damaged-focused rival, [[Zangief Cat (Super Rare Cat)]], who can outright cripple if not delete most Floating enemies just as well as Swimmer and manage peons at the same time with his better range, area attack, and, most importantly, Savage Blow, which once activated, can absolutely obliterate almost every Floating enemy in the game just as effectively if not even better as Swimmer can (240k damage at level 30!). However, due to his much slower speed, higher recharge time, and higher cost, should not be used for rush strategies and in that case would be need to be replaced by Swimmer instead.
If the [[Ototo Corps#Breaker-blast|Breakerblast Cannon]] is not available, Swimmer Cat is also one of the most efficient counters for [[Spacefish Jones]], since it only costs 675¢, can be timed with relative ease, and will continue to deal heavy damage to Jones after destroying its Barrier by exploiting its Floating trait.

==='''True Form'''===
Fishman Cat has its range increased to 215 with more health, damage and movement speed. The added range, even though it might not seem like much, now allows Fishman Cat to outrange all common Bun Bun variants, so timing is no longer needed in such cases. The other improvements good to have in general, as now he moves ''faster'' than [[Crazed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Mohawk]] (at 36 speed to 28) and [[Cow Cat (Normal Cat)|Lion Cat]] (at 36 speed to 30). Their other upgraded stats are also nothing to scoff at, making this unit even stronger than before at what it already does.

==='''Talents'''===
Since this is a Cat that relies a lot on basic stats, the improvements to health and damage, as well as the slot for a [[Talent Orbs|Talent Orb]], preferably Floating, can all contribute to making Fishman Cat much better. Resist Slow is a very situational talent, so unlocking it shouldn't have a high priority. Slow is useless, as Fishman is often used to damage and defeat threats directly, making it irrelevant. Lastly, Move Speed Up. Due to how speed can cause units to clip into enemies slightly, this has the potential of ruining Fishman Cat's gain in range from the True Form, as it becomes unreliable at outranging Bun Bun and his variants, and can also make the unit useless against [[Othom]] since its attack will occur before the Curse effect wears off, though if you can alleviate these issues such as Freezing Bun Buns, Cursing Othom or bringing other units to counter said enemies, this talent is much better to consider since Fishman will get hits in quicker.

==='''Orb'''===
Massive damage against Floating is the best option. If the aforementioned is unavailable, run defense up instead, since an attack up orb provides a much weaker boost comparatively.

