==Trivia==
*[[Version 2.0 Update#Version 2.0.6 Update|Version 2.0.6]] increased Swimmer Cat's range from 155 to 185.
*Prior to [[Version 4.7 Update|Version 4.7]], Swimmer Cat was a part another [[Cat Combo]] called [[Summer by the Sea (Removed Combo)|Summer by the Sea]].
*Prior to [[Version 15.7 Update|Version 15.7]], Swimmer Cat's descriptions read as follows:
<pre>Swimmer Cat
Built from the pain of losing every race.
Obtained its strength from tears of defeat.
Deals massive damage to Floating enemies.</pre>
<pre>Butterfly Cat
Managed to overcome the endless defeat
with great effort. Now blessed with victory!
Deals massive damage to Floating enemies.</pre>
<pre>Fishman Cat
This one can barely even be called a Cat.
Submitted to gene therapy to become the
world champion. Extreme damage to Floating.</pre>
*The lines "Knows the sadness of every match," "Found its strength by crying on its own," and "Won the blessing of victory by facing endless sorrow," in Swimmer Cat's and Butterfly Cat's Japanese descriptions reference the hit single "[[wikipedia:Ultra Soul|Ultra Soul]]" by rock duo [[wikipedia:B'z|B'z]]. The specific lyrics referenced can be translated as "First learn what sadness is, go and cry on your own," and "If you want to be blessed, first let yourself face that endless pain," and are phrased almost exactly like this unit's descriptions in Japanese.
**The song "Ultra Soul" has been associated with competitive swimming in Japan. The [https://youtu.be/Ujb-ZeX7Mo8 music video] takes place at a swimming pool, and one of the single's B-sides is "Suimā-yo 2001!" ("Swimmer-yo 2001!").
*Fishman Cat could be a reference to the [[wikipedia:Gill-man|Gill-man]], a scaly, amphibious humanoid monster from the classic film ''[[wikipedia:Creature from the Black Lagoon|Creature from the Black Lagoon]]''.
**Fishman Cat could also be a reference to the [[wikia:OnePiece:Fish-Men|Fish-Men]] in ''[[wikipedia:One Piece|One Piece]]''.

